# T5.4 case 9 (deferred from T4.2), the half that needs the server away: a
# tab that has just run a statement, a container stopped under it, and the
# Ctrl-R that follows.
#
# scripts/qa/query-workflow.sh waits for `connected.txt`, stops the
# container, and has the ten second wait below to do it in; it starts the
# container again the moment this script is done, so the server is away for
# that wait and the failed connect after it and no longer. The other half —
# Ctrl-R once the container is healthy again — is run-disconnected.keys.

key c
wait busy
expect ●

key Tab
type select count(*) as n from bench.customers
key Ctrl-R
wait busy
expect 50
frame connected

wait 10000
key Ctrl-R
wait busy
expect Results · failed
expect-not Running
frame outage-error
key Ctrl-Q
